{
  "settings": {
    "introImage": {
      "src": "img/lo12/out-and-about-shopping.svg",
      "alt": "Shopping in the market illustration"
    },
    "introHTML": "<p>This lesson teaches how to shop at a French market and use polite exchanges with vendors. Learners practise asking for quantities such as <em>Donnez-moi deux kilos de pommes de terre, s'il vous plaît</em>, checking prices with <em>C'est combien&nbsp;?</em>, and responding to questions such as <em>Avec ça&nbsp;?</em> and <em>C'est tout&nbsp;?</em>.</p><p>It also introduces key vocabulary for shops, food items, quantities, and packaging, alongside useful grammar for <em>aller</em>, partitives and how to say <em>of</em>, and plural forms used when shopping.</p>",
    "informationHTML": "<p><strong>After completing this unit, you will be able to:</strong></p><ul><li>Talk about where you go shopping and describe everyday market routines.</li><li>Ask for quantities politely and ask how much produce costs.</li><li>Use <em>aller</em> accurately in the present tense.</li><li>Choose between <em>du</em>, <em>de la</em>, <em>de l&apos;</em>, <em>des</em>, and <em>de</em> more confidently.</li><li>Hear the difference between the French sounds <em>u</em> and <em>ou</em> and pronounce them correctly.</li></ul>"
  },
  "dialogues": {
    "component": "Section",
    "expandable": false,
    "informationTextHTML": "<p>This section introduces two short market conversations: one about where people shop, and one about buying fruit and vegetables from a market stall.</p>",
    "content": [
      {
        "phraseTable1": {
          "component": "PhraseTable",
          "id": "phraseTable1",
          "informationTextHTML": "<p>Read each phrase, then play its audio clip to check pronunciation and meaning.</p>",
          "phrases": [
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/001-quest-ce-que-tu-fais-aujourdhui.mp3",
              "Qu'est-ce que tu fais aujourd'hui ?",
              "What are you doing today?"
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/002-je-fais-mes-courses.mp3",
              "Je fais mes courses.",
              "I'm doing my shopping."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/003-tu-vas-au-supermarche.mp3",
              "Tu vas au supermarché ?",
              "Are you going to the supermarket?"
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/004-non-je-vais-au-marche-ce-nest-pas-loin-de-chez-moi.mp3",
              "Non, je vais au marché. Ce n'est pas loin de chez moi.",
              "No, I'm going to the market. It isn't very far from me."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/005-cest-bien.mp3",
              "C'est bien !",
              "That's good."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/006-oui-cest-pratique-et-le-jeudi-je-vais-au-grand-marche-au-centre-ville-jachete-so.mp3",
              "Oui, c'est pratique. Et le jeudi, je vais au grand marché au centre-ville. J'achète souvent du fromage et du jambon là-bas. Il y a beaucoup de choix. Et il y a un très bon fleuriste aussi.",
              "Yes, it's practical. And on Thursdays I go to the big market in the town centre. I often buy cheese and ham there. There's lots of choice. And there's a very good florist too."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/007-tu-as-de-la-chance-si-nous-voulons-du-pain-marc-va-a-la-boulangerie-au-bout-de-l.mp3",
              "Tu as de la chance ! Si nous voulons du pain, Marc va à la boulangerie au bout de la rue, mais il n'y a pas de marché près de chez nous. Le samedi matin, Marc et moi allons au supermarché.",
              "You're lucky. If we want bread, Marc goes to the baker's at the end of the road, but there isn't a market near us. On Saturday mornings Marc and I go to the supermarket."
            ]
          ],
          "titleText": "Talking about where you shop",
          "informationTextHTML": "<p>Notice how the speakers talk about where they go shopping and why the market is convenient for them.</p>"
        }
      },
      {
        "phraseTable2": {
          "component": "PhraseTable",
          "id": "phraseTable2",
          "informationTextHTML": "<p>Read each phrase, then play its audio clip to check pronunciation and meaning.</p>",
          "phrases": [
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/008-madame-bonjour-vous-desirez.mp3",
              "Madame, bonjour ! Vous désirez ?",
              "Hello madam! What can I get you?"
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/009-donnez-moi-deux-kilos-de-pommes-de-terre-sil-vous-plait.mp3",
              "Donnez-moi deux kilos de pommes de terre, s'il vous plaît.",
              "Give me two kilos of potatoes please."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/010-avec-ca.mp3",
              "Avec ça ?",
              "Anything else?"
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/011-trois-poireaux-oui-et-deux-poivrons-un-poivron-jaune-et-un-poivron-rouge.mp3",
              "Trois poireaux, oui... et deux poivrons, un poivron jaune et un poivron rouge.",
              "Three leeks, yes... and two peppers, one yellow pepper and one red pepper."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/012-voila-cest-tout.mp3",
              "Voilà ! C'est tout ?",
              "Here you are. Is that everything?"
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/013-les-melons-cest-combien.mp3",
              "Les melons, c'est combien ?",
              "How much are the melons?"
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/014-les-melons-cest-3-euros-la-piece.mp3",
              "Les melons, c'est 3 euros la pièce.",
              "The melons are 3 euros each."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/015-je-vais-prendre-un-melon-et-puis-cest-tout.mp3",
              "Je vais prendre un melon, et puis c'est tout !",
              "I'll take one melon and then that's everything."
            ],
            [
              "audio/lo12/dialogues/016-bien-ca-fait-10-euros-50-sil-vous-plait-madame.mp3",
              "Bien ! Ça fait 10 &euro; 50, s'il vous plaît Madame !",
              "Good! That comes to 10 &euro; 50 please madam."
            ]
          ],
          "titleText": "Buying fruit and vegetables",
          "informationTextHTML": "<p>Listen for the polite request, the quantities ordered, the price question, and the way the sale is completed.</p>"
        }
      }
    ],
